    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both tests pass with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a helper method that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner's email is non-blank, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nThe derivation lives in the existing MapStruct mapper (same place as sibling derived fields like `membershipLevel` and `locality`), so it applies uniformly wherever an owner is mapped to a DTO \u2014 including the `GET /api/owners/{id}` path (`RespondWithOwner`) that the acceptance tests exercise. Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
